{"title":"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Stewart&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Stewart's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">Point</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9fe059ea3506a79afe2df3583a0b5e584fb92d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/3252aaabb4f13cba73818d1df1ee24bfd2998fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 21.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is not on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c30ce254d669cf683eb39f03f05cfdd311f7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the sum of all possible <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeters</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d9c01a214955f96b174391be96b26abf545cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15bb134453eeb3db27cdd27ad65a8176fe0393b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(220); pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.7); pair O=(0,0),A=(-15,0),B=(-6,0),C=(15,0),D=(0,8); D(D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A))--D(MP(&quot;C&quot;,C))--D(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D,NE))--cycle); D(D(MP(&quot;B&quot;,B))--D); D((0,-4)--(0,12),linetype(&quot;4 4&quot;)+linewidth(0.7)); MP(&quot;6&quot;,B/2); MP(&quot;15&quot;,C/2); MP(&quot;9&quot;,(A+B)/2); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"188\" /></center> \n<p>Denote the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61c9d9ea9d9aced9557c9d5355e8b46af45ea6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = AD = CD$\" width=\"117\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/986be899aefe8bc5e4054acfeba042f9966747ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a>, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e82f52473612bdae702daa7d979947b140d1b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 = y^2 - 6^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c564fbb0c5dd48435c65e54696ca8da356587f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2 = x^2 - 15^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/41831aa357d34708065863033cf57ac628c92602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 36 = x^2 - 225 \\Longrightarrow x^2 - y^2 = 189$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" />. The LHS is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59eb5722ed3f69d5d3525dc1e158c45e53b35e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + y)(x - y) = 189$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />. As both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b1ff644df9c7d00ab423df91384f076fa26b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,\\ y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"11\" /> are integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/feaaa2978b56f32e8bc81bbf6358cfd4a0bcb512.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y,\\ x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" /> must be integral divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/a/0da8ff1eb498a98f588d5167cbf270a7067c32a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$189$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>The pairs of divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/a/0da8ff1eb498a98f588d5167cbf270a7067c32a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$189$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c179b18c9871d5e13c52f1e7a05c0c5ab257a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,189)\\ (3,63)\\ (7,27)\\ (9,21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"18\" />. This yields the four potential sets for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258d8c15c5c3451a5286500d18ee72bff098f863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(95,94)\\ (33,30)\\ (17,10)\\ (15,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />. The last is not a possibility since it simply <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Degenerate\" title=\"Degenerate\">degenerates</a> into a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a>. The sum of the three possible perimeters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d5089633eedb7825eff63175cdf34423bc13d7bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(AC) + 2(x_1 + x_2 + x_3) = 90 + 2(95 + 33 + 17) = \\boxed{380}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"444\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>One can also conclude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0ef3be3c175dfe2069e97ed80e5dee2e03bf3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(15,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> doesn't work as it violates the triangle inequality.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Stewart.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Stewart's_Theorem)\">Solution 2 (Stewart's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Stewart&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea6ca1e6b49bfc00a22ac647cc32a7b3c644051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=c$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb16231f5fac101324a9e984086743ad29ca710d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=d$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, then by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">Stewart's Theorem</a> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dcc065a1dbe28d15c0aa71a35bb5a5d629968f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30d^2+21*9*30=9c^2+21c^2=30c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"297\" height=\"16\" />. After simplifying:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e3b2adde48fd724bb274ebadf7de62cb915393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d^2-c^2=189$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The solution follows as above.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drop an altitude from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let the intersection point be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is isosceles, AE is half of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Then, label side AD as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle, you can figure out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac4cdec57e624ace87d67e97a5ed947291f227e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> with adjacent divided by hypotenuse, which in this case is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29653ad37928bfc64cae1bb17b368e5a64eb41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Now we apply law of cosines. Label <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Applying law  of cosines, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d593e199ea92ffe237f620faab4ac49a6925e8d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 = x^2+9^2- 2 \\cdot x \\cdot 9 \\cdot \\cos A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac4cdec57e624ace87d67e97a5ed947291f227e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29653ad37928bfc64cae1bb17b368e5a64eb41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4da65d770ee46923715d59076c5cef2c5fcca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 = x^2+9^2- 2 \\cdot x \\cdot 9 \\cdot \\frac{15}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />, which can be simplified to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f260c0ea0d8cfc2b20f458a74fe4270ccc0fc5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-y^2=189$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. The solution proceeds as the first solution does.\n</p><p>-intelligence_20\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">Stewart's Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I\" title=\"2003 AIME I\">2003 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/w